## Rules (from the Foundation Starter Package, 3-rules.md)

- Reuse before building: run the `reuse-first-audit` skill before planning anything that adds storage.
- Configuration, not code: run the `config-audit` skill before and after each feature.
- History is append-only: retire records, never delete; every change is an event; supersede evidence.
- Never fabricate: missing values show as "not recorded"; no invented numbers or translations.
- No silent failures: a job with no result is failed; nothing is "done" while failures are unreconciled.
- Business questions go to [OWNER] as exact questions, never guessed.
- Agents propose, people decide (growing seeds, approving features, write-backs).
- Every code change goes through the `release-loop` skill; push only when the release log shows every
  feature passed.
- [Public repo? → fictional data only in specs, logs and fixtures.]
- Secrets live in [environment / secret store], never in the repo.

